      "translationChars": 6615,
      "firstParagraph": {
        "source": "The scorching Florida sunshine battered down on my bare shoulders.",
        "translation": "炽热的佛罗里达阳光狠狠地烤在我光裸的肩膀上。",
        "checked": true
      },
      "lastParagraph": {
        "source": "As we pulled out of the driveway, George and Chloe hopping into the front of a cute little silver sedan parked in front of their house, I glanced up into the rearview mirror. Blake stood on the front porch, sighing in annoyance as Isabel tried to climb on top of his shoulders and grab a fistful of his dark hair. So, sure, I was exhausted and sore from spending hours in a tiny airplane seat and sweating like a pig because I had never been in temperatures over sixty-five—but at least I was going to have more fun tonight than Blake Hamilton.",
        "translation": "我们把车开出车道时，乔治和克洛伊也跳上了停在他们家门前的一辆可爱的银色小轿车前座，我瞥了一眼后视镜。布莱克站在前廊上，烦恼地叹着气，而伊莎贝尔正想爬到他肩膀上，一把揪住他的深色头发。所以，没错，我因为在那窄小的飞机座位上坐了好几个小时而疲惫酸痛，又因为从没经历过超过六十五度（华氏）的高温而汗如雨下——但至少今晚，我会比布莱克·汉密尔顿玩得开心。",
        "checked": true
      },
